WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.872 --> 00:00:03.171
Line 3 in hall B is moving.

2
00:00:03.888 --> 00:00:06.129
At its new place it needs more power.

3
00:00:07.146 --> 00:00:08.632
The grid supplies the power.

4
00:00:09.339 --> 00:00:13.286
Through cabinet, transformer and switchboard it reaches the machines.

5
00:00:14.322 --> 00:00:15.495
You are the engineer.

6
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.600
You follow the power from the grid to the line.

7
00:00:19.595 --> 00:00:22.451
That makes seven stations, from the grid to planning.

8
00:00:23.774 --> 00:00:26.351
The first station is the electricity grid.

9
00:00:27.092 --> 00:00:30.041
It brings the power from high voltage into the hall.

10
00:00:31.045 --> 00:00:32.949
At high voltage little is lost.

11
00:00:33.736 --> 00:00:36.743
Only close to the plant does the voltage step down.

12
00:00:37.805 --> 00:00:41.799
You check the capacity map and sign a flexible contract if needed.

13
00:00:42.797 --> 00:00:45.955
Without this you wait in a queue for power in a full area.

14
00:00:47.253 --> 00:00:50.028
The second station is switchgear and protection.

15
00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:53.075
The cabinet switches and guards the power.

16
00:00:54.111 --> 00:00:57.838
In a short circuit only the breaker closest to the fault trips.

17
00:00:58.843 --> 00:01:03.069
The installer sets a protection relay and works with an earthing set.

18
00:01:04.142 --> 00:01:06.685
Without this one fault shuts down the whole hall,

19
00:01:06.847 --> 00:01:08.925
or work on the cabinet is not safe.

20
00:01:10.227 --> 00:01:13.222
The third station is transformers and cables.

21
00:01:13.924 --> 00:01:16.943
The transformer converts the voltage for the machines.

22
00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:20.824
Heat ages it faster, so ribs cool it.

23
00:01:21.575 --> 00:01:23.793
A cable runs on to the switchboard.

24
00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:29.652
You test the oil with a DGA and find cable faults with a reflectometer.

25
00:01:30.696 --> 00:01:33.657
Without this the transformer fails unexpectedly,

26
00:01:33.842 --> 00:01:35.909
or you search long for a cable fault.

27
00:01:37.279 --> 00:01:40.193
The fourth station is motors and fluid power.

28
00:01:40.915 --> 00:01:43.330
The motor drives the belt of line 3.

29
00:01:44.309 --> 00:01:46.399
The compressor compresses air for the line.

30
00:01:47.142 --> 00:01:50.033
That is costly energy, and leaks waste power.

31
00:01:51.051 --> 00:01:54.940
You measure the motor current with a clamp meter and run a leak test.

32
00:01:55.953 --> 00:02:00.481
Without this the air leaks away and an oversized motor runs at half load.

33
00:02:01.856 --> 00:02:04.688
The fifth station is pumps, flow and heat.

34
00:02:05.444 --> 00:02:08.672
A pump feeds the product from the tank to the filling unit.

35
00:02:09.715 --> 00:02:11.909
Pump and pipe together fix the flow.

36
00:02:12.661 --> 00:02:15.772
A heat exchanger passes on heat without mixing.

37
00:02:16.793 --> 00:02:19.928
You read the pump curve and pick a plate heat exchanger.

38
00:02:20.967 --> 00:02:24.868
Without this the pump runs at the wrong point and energy is lost.

39
00:02:26.228 --> 00:02:29.688
The sixth station is grid operations and assets.

40
00:02:30.395 --> 00:02:33.565
The grid operator upgrades the connection of the plant.

41
00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:39.169
After that it watches the grid, fixes outages and steers when it is full.

42
00:02:40.178 --> 00:02:43.696
It runs a readiness check and switches by a switching plan.

43
00:02:44.696 --> 00:02:47.018
Without this the connection takes longer and

44
00:02:47.065 --> 00:02:49.770
the power drops unexpectedly during work.

45
00:02:51.119 --> 00:02:54.312
The seventh station is grid planning and the transition.

46
00:02:55.032 --> 00:02:58.167
The planner looks at how much power is needed later.

47
00:02:59.193 --> 00:03:03.164
Demand grows, so he works out where and when the grid fills up.

48
00:03:04.193 --> 00:03:06.887
He runs a load flow for each scenario.

49
00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:12.315
Without this the upgrade comes too late and the next line waits for power.

50
00:03:13.685 --> 00:03:14.811
This is the whole map.

51
00:03:15.588 --> 00:03:18.003
The seven stations lie in one zone.

52
00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:22.353
First the electricity grid, from power to congestion.

53
00:03:23.451 --> 00:03:27.700
Then switchgear and protection, from switching devices to safe switching.

54
00:03:28.788 --> 00:03:32.875
Then transformers and cables, from the transformer to connections.

55
00:03:33.966 --> 00:03:37.936
Then motors and fluid power, from plant energy to hydraulics.

56
00:03:39.006 --> 00:03:42.245
Then pumps, flow and heat, from pipes to steam.

57
00:03:43.355 --> 00:03:47.882
Then grid operations and assets, from request to congestion management.

58
00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:52.968
Finally grid planning and the transition, from load to flexibility.

59
00:03:53.979 --> 00:03:55.384
That is how they connect.

60
00:03:56.114 --> 00:04:01.187
The grid supplies, the switchgear protects and the transformer converts the voltage.

61
00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.109
Motors and pumps use the power.

62
00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:08.301
Operations and planning keep the grid able to supply it.

63
00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:12.611
Each station is a module with four levels per topic.

64
00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.618
Start with what touches your line most.
